    "lawCode": "Add §91, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6856\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the state law, in relation to\ndesignating \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" the official state hymn of\nmourning in honor of all American veterans\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to designate \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\"\ncomposed by Donald Miller as the official state hymn for the Unknown\nSoldier.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nAmends the state law to designate \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" as the\nofficial state hymn for the Unknown Soldier.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nNone\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nDesignation of \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" as the official state\nhymn for the Unknown Soldier will provide recognition and\nacknowledgement of the many sacrifices made by veterans in defense of\nour state and nation. This song is designated because it specifically\nwas written in honor of the Unknown Soldier. \"Here Rests in Honored\nGlory\" is based on the inscription on the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nS6540/A8021 of 1990/Passed Senate.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
