    "lawCode": "Add §91, State L",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6856A\n\nSPONSOR: DEFRANCISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to designating \"Here Rests in\nHonored Glory\" the official state hymn of remembrance in honor of all\nAmerican veterans\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to designate \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\"\ncomposed by Donald Miller as the official state hymn for the Unknown\nSoldier.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends the state law to designate \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" as the\nofficial state hymn for the Unknown Soldier.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDesignation of \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" as the official state hymn\nfor the Unknown Soldier will provide recognition and acknowledgement of\nthe many sacrifices made by veterans in defense of our state and nation.\nThis song is designated because it specifically was written in honor of\nthe Unknown Soldier. \"Here Rests in Honored Glory\" is based on the\ninscription on the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS6540/A8021 of 1990/Passed Senate.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
